  # wrapU 0 is REPEAT and wrapV 1 is CLAMP, and both matter.
  #
  # Across: the quad is several tiles wide and the material repeats the texture over it, so
  # clamped horizontally -- which is what this said until the tiling went in -- the layer
  # would be one tile followed by its last column of pixels smeared over the rest of the
  # quad. That is a worse artefact than the stretched single image it replaces, and it looks
  # like a mistake in the drawing rather than in the import, which is the hardest kind to
  # find. ridge() is built to wrap for the same reason.
  #
  # Up and down: nothing repeats vertically and clamping there keeps the top row of sky from
  # bleeding into the bottom row of ground through the mip chain.
